# DTF tier manifest: pypi-remote-index-path
#   (artifact-keeper#5643, 1.12.4)
# Profile-set: filesystem + upstreams.mock-files (a stdlib-python upstream at
# 172.16.<slot>.76 whose files and forced statuses the oracle sets over its
# control API on the slot's TRIVY_PORT).
#
# The mock stands in for a flat-layout index such as
# https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu: the project page is at
# /idx/<project>/, and /idx/simple/<project>/ answers 403, as that CDN does.
#
# THE BUGS (#5643)
#   1. A PyPI Remote pointed at such an index with the default index path
#      ("simple") answered `502 Failed to fetch from upstream` with nothing
#      naming the cause; the upstream 403 was only in the backend log, and
#      the `pypi_upstream_index_path` setting that fixes it was undocumented.
#      Fixed: the generic proxy 502 carries `X-AK-Upstream-Status: <status>`
#      (body unchanged), and docs/pypi-remote.md documents the setting.
#   2. PEP 691 content negotiation was a substring check that ignored
#      q-values: `Accept: application/vnd.pypi.simple.latest+json` got HTML,
#      and `v1+json;q=0.1, text/html` (HTML preferred) got JSON. Fixed: q
#      values and the `latest` alias are read; a tie still goes to JSON.
#
# THE GATES
#   (CONTROL) both images: with `pypi_upstream_index_path: ""` the Remote
#     serves the flat index; with the default it answers 502 with the
#     unchanged "Failed to fetch from upstream" body. pip's and uv's Accept
#     header gets JSON, `text/html` and `*/*` get HTML (project page and the
#     root index of a hosted repository).
#   (FIX) #5643: the 502 carries `X-AK-Upstream-Status: 403`; `latest+json`
#     gets JSON and `v1+json;q=0.1, text/html` gets HTML. RED on sha-30a358c.
#
# Item 3 of #5643 (repo_selector on /users/{id}/tokens) is gated in
# token-repo-restriction.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: requests back to back.
# UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS=true: the mock upstream is on a private subnet.
COVERS="5643"
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-files"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
